    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Whitt Seminary was founded in 1880 by Christian Church elders, building a community school on five acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitt%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the mid‑1880s, Whitt boasted a weekly newspaper called the Whitt Moon, three churches, and twenty businesses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitt%2C_Texas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Settlement began in the early to mid‑1870s, turning Whitt into a retail and social hub for farmers on the stage line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitt%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Like other Parker County towns bypassed by railroads, Whitt began to decline in the early 1900s, with the Great Depression accelerating the fall.",
